@startuml sequence-diagram-matching
/'
  AI Usage Note
  Drafted with Claude; updated to match matching.md, notifications.md,
  data-model.md, UC-001 and high-level-design.md (I1, I3).
'/
title Nearby — Sequence Diagram: Matching (main success scenario, UC-001)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
autonumber

actor "User" as U
participant "Expo App" as APP
participant "Main Server\n(API + job handlers)" as SRV
database "PostgreSQL\n(tables + job queue)" as DB
participant "Expo Push" as PUSH
actor "Candidate" as C

== Apply ==

U -> APP : apply to event session
APP -> SRV : POST /sessions/{id}/applications
SRV -> DB : insert application (in_pool)
SRV --> APP : 202 Accepted — in pool, next round at …

== Scheduled round ==

DB ->> SRV : matching.round job
SRV -> SRV : match(pool, exclusions, seed)\nin a worker thread
SRV -> DB : in one transaction: Match (proposed),\ninbox rows, deliver + expire jobs
SRV ->> PUSH : push "match proposed"
PUSH ->> APP : notification
PUSH ->> C : notification

== Both accept ==

U -> APP : accept
APP -> SRV : POST /matches/{id}/accept
SRV -> DB : match → accepted_a
C -> SRV : accept (from the candidate's app)
SRV -> DB : match → mutual; inbox rows (match_mutual)

== Contact reveal ==

APP -> SRV : GET /matches/{id}
SRV -> DB : check mutual + safety notice acknowledged
SRV --> APP : contact details (FR-019)

note over SRV
  Server-side checks: per-session lock (FUNC-002),
  403 unless mutual (SEC-001), contacts only after
  the safety notice (SAFE-002).
end note

note over U, C
  Not shown — see UC-001 and matching.md: instant match on apply (rule 1),
  decline (A3), expiry and strikes (A4, rule 6), withdrawal (A5), open mode.
end note

@enduml
